                <pb facs="0098" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg42"/>

                <head>No. 31.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gonzalez Errazuriz to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Chili</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Philadelphia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11, 1876</date>.
                        (Received June 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, in the name of the
                    minister, to acknowledge the receipt of your excellency’s communication of the
                    5th instant, and, in accordance with your desire expressed therein, to inform
                    you that wool, both carded and uncarded, is exempt from all customs duties in
                    Chili, and is imported and exported freely.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRANCISCO GONZALEZ ERRAZURIZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
